Backend — data model (high level)

EntityKey            fields
User             id, name, email, password_hash, role
Wallet           id, user_id, cash_balance, gold_grams_balance
Investment       id, user_id, amount, status, created_at
Transaction      id, user_id, type (credit/debit), amount,ref_id, created_at


Backend — weekly schedule (6 weeks)

Week 1 — Foundation & Auth


Project scaffolding (Spring Boot, DB config, environment profiles: dev/prod)
User entity, registration, login, JWT-based auth, password hashing
Role support (CUSTOMER, ADMIN) for later admin endpoints
Deliverable: /auth/register, /auth/login working end to end, Postman collection


Week 2 — Wallet & Dashboard


Wallet entity (cash balance + gold grams balance), created automatically on signup
Transaction entity + ledger write path
Dashboard API: current balance, grams held, recent transactions, progress toward next redeemable item
Deliverable: GET /wallet, GET /transactions (paginated, filterable by type/date)


Week 3 — Investment & Payment


InvestmentPlan seed data (Monthly Saver, Flexi, Lumpsum)
Investment entity + /invest endpoint (validate amount, create pending investment)
Payment integration — start with a mock/sandbox provider (e.g. Razorpay/Stripe test mode) so the flow is real without live money
On successful payment: credit Transaction, update Wallet.cash_balance or grams depending on your product decision (cash-first vs. grams-first — needs a client decision, see open questions below)
Deliverable: POST /invest, POST /payments/confirm, webhook handler for payment provider


Week 4 — Redemption Request


RedemptionRequest entity + /redeem/request endpoint (user picks amount/grams + requested date)
Validation: requested amount ≤ available balance, requested date ≥ today
Status transitions: pending → scheduled
Deliverable: POST /redeem/request, GET /redeem/requests (user's own requests + status)

Week 5 — Admin, Notifications, Reporting


Admin views: pending redemption requests, daily rate entry screen, order fulfilment status updates
Notifications (email at minimum) on: payment success, redemption purchased, order status change
Basic reporting: total AUM, total grams held across users, redemption volume
Deliverable: admin API set + notification hooks


Week 6 — Hardening & Deployment


Security review (JWT expiry/refresh, rate limiting on auth, input validation everywhere)
Move H2 → real DB (Postgres/MySQL) for staging/prod, externalize secrets
Load/edge-case testing on the redemption→purchase scheduled job (this is the riskiest piece — money and gold both move here)
CI/CD pipeline, deploy to staging
Deliverable: staging environment live, test coverage on core money-movement paths